Third-party work
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

colibri
  https://github.com/JustVugg/colibri
  Copyright Vincenzo Fornaro. Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
  The GLM-5.2 engine (web/glm/, tools/glm_*.py) uses colibri's technique, which
  keeps the dense part of a mixture-of-experts model resident and streams the
  routed experts from disk. It also reads colibri's int4/int8 container format
  and its .coli_usage routing history. The code here is an independent WebGPU
  and NumPy implementation; no colibri source is included.

GPT-2 byte-pair encoding
  https://github.com/openai/gpt-2
  Copyright (c) 2019 OpenAI. Licensed under a modified MIT License.
  web/bpe.js reimplements the GPT-2 encoder's byte-to-unicode mapping and
  merge procedure.

UMAP
  https://github.com/lmcinnes/umap
  Copyright (c) 2017, Leland McInnes. Licensed under the BSD 3-Clause License.
  The data-set tools use umap-learn to build the layouts. kernel/umap.c and
  web/umap.js are an independent implementation of the algorithm (McInnes,
  Healy and Melville, 2018).

Models and data
  The repository contains no model weights or data sets. The tools fetch them
  from their publishers, and each comes under its own licence, which the viewer
  shows:
  - GPT-2: OpenAI, MIT License.
  - DistilGPT2: Hugging Face, Apache License 2.0.
  - MDLM: Sahoo et al., Kuleshov Group, Cornell, Apache License 2.0.
  - GLM-5.2: Z.ai, MIT License.
  - GPT-2 sparse autoencoders: Joseph Bloom, MIT License. Feature descriptions
    are fetched live from Neuronpedia (https://www.neuronpedia.org).
  - Jina-CLIP-v2: Jina AI, CC BY-NC 4.0. It produced the vectors of the
    KnowDrive store data set.

